@startuml wt_digging_failover
title WT failover during DIGGING
hide footbox
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 75
participant "Boomlet A" as A
participant "Boomlet B" as B
participant "Other three Boomlets" as P
participant "STs" as ST
participant "Old WT" as Old
participant "Candidate WT" as C
participant "Bound SARs" as S

opt Partial delivery of an old Pong round
  Old -> A: Valid old-head Pong and own exact SAR acknowledgment
  A -> A: Apply ordinary counter and bounded height rules
  Old -x B: Pong unavailable
  B -> B: Retain outstanding Ping and previous counter
end

opt A duress challenge was required by an accepted Pong
  A -> ST: Retained nonce-bound challenge before freeze
  ST -> A: User response
  A -> A: Bind answer to exact next ordinary placeholder before freeze
end

ref over A,C
  02_common_switch.puml
  Five reviewed snapshots preserve DIGGING and report predecessor heights.
  Discharge every frozen placeholder before initial PREPARE.
  Install the candidate only after a final ACTIVATE certificate.
end ref

alt Final ABORT
  A -> A: Retain original head, accepted increment and obligations
  B -> B: Retain original head and outstanding Ping
else Final ACTIVATE
  note over A,P
    Frozen obligations were discharged before PREPARE.
    Installation preserves those discharges and all private delay state.
  end note

  group One recovery Ping per installed head
    A -> A: Persist next signed padded Ping with fresh placeholder IV
    B -> B: Persist next signed padded Ping with fresh placeholder IV
    A -> C: Recovery Ping with next sequence and retained reached flag
    B -> C: Recovery Ping with next sequence and retained reached flag
    P -> C: Three corresponding fresh recovery Pings
    note over A,P
      Recovery creation leaves counters and heights unchanged.
      Crash retries send identical retained Ping bytes.
    end note
    C -> S: Forward every new exact placeholder
    S -> C: Each encrypted exact SAR acknowledgment
  end

  alt All five fresh Pings have reached flags
    C -> A: Current-head reached collection and own exact SAR acknowledgment
    C -> B: Current-head reached collection and own exact SAR acknowledgment
    C -> P: Current-head reached collection and each own exact SAR acknowledgment
    A -> A: Verify five reached Pings and own exact acknowledgment before signing
    B -> B: Verify five reached Pings and own exact acknowledgment before signing
  else At least one peer is still digging
    C -> C: Respect maximum inherited predecessor height plus spacing
    C -> A: Head-scoped Pong with four peer Pings and own SAR acknowledgment
    C -> B: Head-scoped Pong with four peer Pings and own SAR acknowledgment
    C -> P: Recipient-specific Pongs and own acknowledgments
    A -> A: Verify strict sequences, heights, scope, spacing and exact acknowledgment
    B -> B: Verify strict sequences, heights, scope, spacing and exact acknowledgment
    A -> A: Apply ordinary counter predicate and bounded catch-up
    B -> B: Apply ordinary counter predicate and bounded catch-up
    ref over A,ST
      Each peer performs its ordinary per-round duress draw,
      completes any selected challenge, and creates its next ordinary Ping.
    end ref
  end
end
@enduml
